  "body": "### Describe the bug\n\nWhen configuring a Tracearr integration, Homarr repeatedly generates malformed DNS queries where the protocol string (https) is appended to the hostname. This results in DNS lookups like:\n\ntracearr.mydomain.nethttps\n\nThis causes continuous DNSSEC validation failures and SERVFAIL responses from the DNS server.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Add a Tracearr integration in Homarr\n2. Set URL to: https://tracearr.mydomain.net\n3. Save and enable integration\n4. Add Tracearr widget to dashboard\n5. Observe DNS logs on upstream resolver (Blocky in this case)\n\n### Impact\n\nExcessive query load on DNS.\n\n### Additional information\n\n<img width=\"1247\" height=\"746\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c4796455-5d77-476f-a06f-773c6a821ce1\" />\n\n### Version\n\n1.56.1\n\n### Installation method\n\nDocker Compose\n\n### Browser\n\nBrave",
